description:
This is a combined synopsis/solicitation for commercial items prepared in accordance with the format in FAR Part 12.&nbsp; This announcement constitutes the only solicitation.&nbsp; Quotations are being requested and a separate written solicitation will not be issued.&nbsp; 

Solicitation number 127EAT27Q0004 is issued as a Request for Quotation (RFQ) for Airport BAER Weed Survey and Treatment. 

This acquisition&nbsp; is set-aside for small business concerns.&nbsp; The applicable North American Industry Classification Standard Code is 115310&nbsp; The small business size standard is $11.5M &nbsp;This acquisition is a Total Small Business Set-Aside.&nbsp; All responsible sources may submit a quotation which will be considered by the agency.&nbsp; 

 Statement of Requirement  

The purpose of this project is to procure services to survey and treat target non-native plants in areas affected by the 2024 Airport Fire. The contractor will survey and treat up to 200 acres of areas impacted by the Airport Fire on the Trabuco Ranger District of the Cleveland National Forest. Survey and treatment areas will include: trails, meadow areas, Forest road sides, riparian areas, chaparral, and campgrounds. Surveys and treatments will prioritize known non-native weed infestations that were impacted by the fire and fire suppression activities. 

Period of Performance for this requirement is date of award through 30 September 2027.&nbsp; 

Quotes shall be submitted to megan.acord@usda.gov and are due no later than November 30, 2026 at 12:00 PM MT. Please include the solicitation name and number as the subject line of the email.&nbsp; 

 Questions  

Questions shall be submitted via email to megan.acord@usda.gov and are due no later than November 23, 2025, at 12:00 PM Pacific Time.&nbsp; This will ensure enough time to respond before the solicitation period ends.&nbsp; Please include the solicitation name and number as the subject line of the email. 

